 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Ya'qub and Yusuf: no plate. Geometric for «إلى الله وأعلم من الله…» and «إن الله يجزي المتصدقين», light for «روح الله» (nothing on the negated «ولا تيأسوا»). 89:1-7 is not glossed. 87:12-20 keeps «لا ييأس… إلا القوم الكافرون» whole. STAGING v4: c1 (86-87) at Ya'qub's tents in the desert (12:100): Ya'qub is only a blue drop labelled Ya'qub; his sons are a plain group of three (3 figures = a group, not their number). He answers them (86:1, 86:8) and his drop dips once, softly, as he speaks of his grief (86:3; no weeping, nothing on his eyes); a geometric plate for to Allah and from Allah (86:6-13). He tells them to go and seek news (87:1); nothing on the negated do not despair (87:7-9), a geometric plate for Allah's relief (87:10-12; geometric, not light, on a word of His mercy); the sons (plain figures, never the rejecting crowd) leave the stage at 87:12 (they went, 88), so only Ya'qub's drop stands while the disbelieving people are named (87:13-20) and no figure is seen as them. c2 (88-89) in the town of Egypt: the brothers come in with their camel and walk to Yusuf (88:2, they entered upon him), who is only a blue drop labelled Yusuf at the right. They plead (88:4, 88:9, 88:13; no bowing toward the drop); a coins plate for their poor price (88:11-12, Al-Muyassar: poor, few dirhams) and a geometric plate for Allah rewards the charitable (88:18). Yusuf answers them (89:1, 89:5, 89:9); no glow or light on him."
 },
